 "sentences": [
  {
   "s": 0.0,
   "e": 5.02,
   "text": "Five goals at once usually means zero progress. Think about it, with work and everything else,"
  },
  {
   "s": 5.2,
   "e": 9.98,
   "text": "you've got maybe five or six free hours a week. Split that five ways and each goal gets about an"
  },
  {
   "s": 9.98,
   "e": 14.78,
   "text": "hour. That's not enough to move any of them. So pick one main goal for the next 12 weeks,"
  },
  {
   "s": 15.06,
   "e": 20.34,
   "text": "just one. Say it's launching a side business. That goal gets your five best hours every week,"
  },
  {
   "s": 20.72,
   "e": 24.96,
   "text": "not whatever leftover time you have at the end of the day. The other goals don't disappear,"
  },
  {
   "s": 25.3,
   "e": 28.92,
   "text": "they go on the minimum, just enough to keep them alive. So if you're a runner,"
  },
  {
   "s": 28.92,
   "e": 33.44,
   "text": "you're not training for a race right now. You do two easy runs a week and you keep your fitness."
  },
  {
   "s": 33.96,
   "e": 38.32,
   "text": "And anything you can't even do the minimum for, park it on a list with a date like January 1st,"
  },
  {
   "s": 38.58,
   "e": 43.18,
   "text": "when you'll look at it again. Because one goal that's actually moving beats five goals that"
  },
  {
   "s": 43.18,
   "e": 48.14,
   "text": "are all stuck. That's what Demure is for. You archive your dream today so you can see it"
  },
  {
   "s": 48.14,
   "e": 52.94,
   "text": "tomorrow and break it down into small steps you can actually do. If you want to try it out,"
  },
  {
   "s": 52.94,
   "e": 54.28,
   "text": "I've put the link in the bio."
  }
 ],
